CFG659: does the settling field P leave any signature in ordinary matter or light?

Criteria: FROZEN_CRITERIA.md (committed alone, 75e95fe06). Reading lane on CFG694 (action), CFG695 (saturating W), CFG696
(radiative attractor); no CFG690-699 file is edited or imported.
  L = -|grad Phi - 4 pi G lam P|^2 / 8 pi G - rho_b Phi - W(P) - (gamma/2)|grad P|^2 + (I/2)|P_t|^2      (lam = 1 is the action)
  gamma = 2 pi G L*^2  (CFG691: l_gamma = L*^2 / 2 r_M);  c_P = sqrt(gamma / I) unfixed (CFG696).
  W: CFG695 saturating vacuum minus the critical quadratic; in u = 4 pi G P:  4 pi G W = w(u) = -a0 u - a0^2 ln(1 - u/a0) - u^2/2,
     w'(u) = u^2/(a0 - u),  w''(u) = u(2 a0 - u)/(a0 - u)^2.   Local gap for P perturbations: m^2 = 4 pi G w''/gamma = 2 w''/L*^2.
kappa = 1/2 FITTED; footings 9.3603e-11 / 1.1312e-10 never pooled; cold energy mass required; no particle species; not
"theory closed"; no LCDM or standard-MOND yardstick in any verdict.

Run:  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 nice -n 10 python3 cfg659.py        (CFG659_MUTATE=1: lam = 0; exit 1 iff any channel is non-zero)

D1  coupling: Phi equation div(grad Phi - 4 pi G lam P) = 4 pi G rho_b  =>  g = g_N - 4 pi G lam P_L;  P_T never enters Phi
  [PASS] D1 g = g_N - 4piG lam P_L exactly; a purely transverse P leaves Phi unchanged: max|g - (g_N - 4piG lam P_L)| = 0.0e+00; max|Phi[P_T] - Phi_N| = 0.0e+00
    Matter feels P ONLY through Phi (universal, composition-blind): a passing longitudinal wave gives delta a = -4 pi G lam delta P_L.
    Electromagnetism: the action has NO term containing A_mu or F_munu. Any direct P-light coupling would be a NEW TERM (a knob);
    none is added. Light sees P only through the metric potentials (Phi; Psi = Phi is the open relativistic completion).

D2  linear waves about a background u0 (a0 = footing):
    longitudinal:  I w^2 = gamma (k^2 + m^2),  m^2 = 2 w''(u0)/L*^2   (the |grad Phi - 4piG P|^2 term is P_L-independent: no mass)
    transverse:    I w^2 = gamma k^2 + 4 pi G lam^2 + gamma m_T^2         (massive, and decoupled from matter by D1)
    speed c_P = sqrt(gamma/I) (unfixed, CFG696). These are NOT GR gravitational waves: longitudinal, speed c_P, gapped where u0 != 0.
    regimes: deep (u0 << a0) m^2 = 4 u0/(a0 L*^2);  saturated (g >> a0) m ~ sqrt2 g/(a0 L*);  screened core of a star: u0 ~ GM/L*^2 ~ 0.
D3  traveling longitudinal wave: e = I Pdot^2, flux F = c_P e;  delta u0 = 4 pi G lam delta P0 = lam sqrt(16 pi G c_P F)/(w L*)

K1  static field energy of CFG696's functional (cubic W): E_code(S) = -int_0^S [v'^2/2 + v^2/s^2 + |v|^3/(3s) - v/s] ds
    lam = 0: E_code(200) = -0.000e+00

S1  energy released by settling, saturating W (framework-native): E = M_b V_f^2 * eps(R/r_M),  V_f^4 = G M_b a0, r_M = sqrt(G M_b/a0)
